246
00:14:58,620 --> 00:14:59,680
Not for long!

247
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:04,660
I sacrificed my Swordsman of
Landstar to summon maximum six!

248
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:11,040
Now whatever number I roll is multiplied
by 200 and add it to his attack points.

249
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:17,340
Looks like he gets an extra 1,200 points.

250
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:23,660
And since I'm feeling lucky, I'll
play my Star Blaster Magic card.

251
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:27,760
The higher he rolls, the
stronger a monster I can play.

252
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:31,080
But first, I have to
sacrifice my Suzuki Samurai.

253
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:33,680
And away we go!

254
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:37,490
Nice!

255
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:41,480
Since my samurai had two
stars and I rolled a five,

256
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:43,956
I get to summon a seven-star monster.

257
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,820
So go, red eyes, red dragon!

258
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:54,380
Now, Maximum Six, take out his
Valkyrie with lightning fist attack!

259
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:58,380
No way!

260
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:00,120
Why wasn't she destroyed?

261
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:02,580
It's called a special ability.

262
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Brunhilde avoids destruction by
giving up a thousand defense points.

263
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:09,730
Fine!

264
00:16:09,813 --> 00:16:10,716
All right, red eyes!

265
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,580
You get rid of us with Inferno Fire Blast!

266
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:23,460
Then I'll activate my
Type 6 machine again.

267
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:29,357
I've embarrassed you enough, so I'll
place this space down and call it quits.

268
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:32,760
With only a hundred points
left, this is your last shot!

269
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:36,840
Nice comeback, dude! You rock! Good job!

270
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:42,674
You should have ended this
duel when you had the chance.

271
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:45,180
Now prepare to pay the price.

272
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,900
This duel's gone on long enough,

273
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:54,700
so I activate the magic card
Enchanted Sword Noothout!

274
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:58,040
It raises Brunhild's attack
points by four hundred!

275
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:05,700
According to the legend of Nothung, it
was the world's greatest dragon slayer.

276
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:07,240
Say what? It's true.

277
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:12,920
With one fell swoop, this sword can
remove every single dragon from play.

278
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:15,980
Not my red eyes!

279
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:20,740
Next I play my final card
and the key to my victory.

280
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,557
Rainbow Bridge Bifrost.

281
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:29,580
So my Valkyrie gains 500 attack points
for every monster I remove from the game.

282
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:30,760
Now I get it.

283
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:34,249
He's been planning this
from the beginning.

284
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:37,177
That's why Siegfried removed
all of Joey's monsters.

285
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:39,140
To power up his own.

286
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:45,184
Now his Valkyrie is strong enough
to wipe out Joey's life points.

287
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,160
Hold your horsey.

288
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:52,660
I play compensation mediation.

289
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:56,200
So, you're relying on luck again?

290
00:17:56,360 --> 00:18:00,337
Look, pal, I think you're scared
because I never lose at these things.

291
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:02,937
Now choose any two cards
from your graveyard and

292
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:05,961
shuffle them together with
my Mediation Trap card.

293
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:09,320
Then I get to pick one card.

294
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,260
And if I choose mine, I'm safe.

295
00:18:12,380 --> 00:18:16,300
Yes, and should you fail,
then I win the duel.

296
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,180
I know you can do this.

297
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:23,097
And the card I pick is...

298
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,740
The middle one

299
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:31,300
Oh, no!

300
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:40,360
It looks like your luck has run out
Now, Hilda, my dear End this duel

301
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:49,940
No way!

302
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,157
This can't be!

303
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,280
He lost!

304
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:58,680
Herr Joseph, some things
in life just never change.

305
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:03,180
A rose is a rose, and a loser is a loser.

306
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:08,000
And the winner of this
bout is Siegfried Lloyd!

307
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:13,060
And with that, the grand championship
is down to its final four duelists.

308
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:15,360
Big deal.

309
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,817
So you blew the entire tournament
on a lousy game of chance.

310
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:21,429
I guess you must have
just run out of luck.

311
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:25,652
Nah, Joey wins his duels with
talent, not with luck, guys.

312
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:28,057
Oh, so Joey didn't lose
because he has no luck.

313
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:30,081
He lost because he has no talent.

314
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:32,200
So that's how you cheer me up?

315
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:35,893
Then it's time for me to spread
a little cheer on my own!

316
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:40,400
Joey did a great job.

317
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:44,357
And sooner or later, he's going to
learn to control that temper of his.

318
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,760
Probably later.

319
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:48,000
I get no respect at all!
